-- Insurance Contracts Act 1984 (Cth) with the Insurance Contracts Regulations 2017, the insured's questions -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. The Insurance Contracts Regulations 2017 are deposited and are read here.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_insurance-contracts-act-1984_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts are from the workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe/facts.json, event c04a (15 September 2026):
-- Chloe, 23, takes income protection and life cover inside her super fund. That the cover is a group life contract
-- with the trustee as insured, that she opted in and became a life insured that day, and every health fact, answer,
-- premium and sum insured are HYPOTHETICAL: the life does not state them.

