§ `c04a -- what may the insurer do if Chloe carelessly misstated her health (ss 29, 32)`

#ASSERT `What may the insurer do because of my relevant failure` `Chloe's death cover in her super fund` TRUE FALSE `a contract on other terms or for a higher premium` FALSE (Date 15 9 2026) (Date 1 3 2028) EQUALS `reduce the sum insured to no less than the s 29(4) formula sum, and only within 3 years (s 29(10))`
#ASSERT `What may the insurer do because of my relevant failure` `Chloe's death cover in her super fund` TRUE FALSE `a contract on other terms or for a higher premium` FALSE (Date 15 9 2026) (Date 16 9 2029) EQUALS `nothing: 3 years have passed on cover with a surrender value or for death (s 29(10))`
#ASSERT `What may the insurer do because of my relevant failure` `Chloe's death cover in her super fund` TRUE FALSE `no contract with me on any terms` FALSE (Date 15 9 2026) (Date 15 9 2029) EQUALS `avoid the contract, within 3 years, because it would not have insured me on any terms (s 29(3))`
#ASSERT `What may the insurer do because of my relevant failure` `Chloe's income protection in her super fund` TRUE FALSE `no contract with me on any terms` FALSE (Date 15 9 2026) (Date 1 3 2031) EQUALS `reduce the sum insured to no less than the s 29(4) formula sum, or vary the contract to where it would have been (s 29(6))`

§ `s 28 -- general insurance`

#ASSERT `What may the insurer do because of my relevant failure` `a home contents policy` TRUE FALSE `a contract on other terms or for a higher premium` FALSE (Date 1 7 2027) (Date 1 7 2035) EQUALS `reduce what it pays on a claim to where it would have been without the failure (s 28(3))`

§ `s 29(4), s 30 -- the SP / Q formula and a misstated date of birth (reg 10: 11%)`

#ASSERT `What is the least sum insured the insurer may substitute` 500000 1000 1250 EQUALS 400000

#ASSERT `What happens because my date of birth was misstated` 100000 900 1000 EQUALS `the insurer may reduce the sum insured to no less than the standard formula sum, at any time`
#ASSERT `What happens because my date of birth was misstated` 100000 1100 1000 EQUALS `the insurer must refund overpaid premium with interest at 11% a year, or raise the sum insured to the standard formula sum`

§ `ss 20B(5A), 21(3A), 25A, 33F, 33H, reg 13A -- genetic testing and life insurance (from 8 October 2026)`

#ASSERT `Is this protected genetic information` `a BRCA1 test result`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this protected genetic information` `my mother's diagnosed type 1 diabetes, by name`
#ASSERT `Is this protected genetic information` `my mother's diagnosed Huntington disease, before any symptoms`

-- c04a: Chloe became a life insured on 15 September 2026, before the protections commenced on 8 October 2026.
#ASSERT `Must I tell my life insurer about genetic testing` TRUE (Date 15 9 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the 2026 protections do not reach my contract: the ordinary disclosure rules decide`
#ASSERT `Must I tell my life insurer about genetic testing` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `nothing: not telling it is neither a breach of the duty of disclosure nor a misrepresentation`

#ASSERT `May my life insurer ask for or use my protected genetic information` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: using it is an offence (60 penalty units) and a contravention (civil penalty 5,000 penalty units) (s 33H)`
#ASSERT `May my life insurer ask for or use my protected genetic information` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I gave it unasked and consented in writing, and its use did not disadvantage me (s 33H(3))`
#ASSERT `May my life insurer ask for or use my protected genetic information` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Division 5 does not reach this decision (Sch 1 item 4)`

