#ASSERT `May the insurer rely on this term against me` `an ordinary exclusion`
#ASSERT NOT `May the insurer rely on this term against me` `an ordinary exclusion relied on in bad faith`
#ASSERT NOT `May the insurer rely on this term against me` `an unusual term never pointed out`
#ASSERT NOT `May the insurer rely on this term against me` `an arbitration clause in the policy`
#ASSERT NOT `May the insurer rely on this term against me` `a pre-existing condition exclusion, the condition unknown to Chloe`
#ASSERT `May the insurer rely on this term against me` `a pre-existing condition exclusion, the condition known to Chloe`
#ASSERT NOT `May the insurer rely on this term against me` `a pre-existing condition exclusion in a 2027 life policy, only a gene variant known`

#ASSERT `What is the least my home insurer may pay me despite an average provision` 20000 60000 100000 EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `What is the least my home insurer may pay me despite an average provision` 100000 60000 100000 EQUALS 60000

§ `s 54 -- something done after the contract; a late claim`

#ASSERT `May the insurer refuse my claim because of what happened after the contract` `a claim notified after the policy's 30-day limit` EQUALS `no: it may only reduce the claim by the prejudice it suffered (s 54(1))`
#ASSERT `May the insurer refuse my claim because of what happened after the contract` `leaving the burglar alarm off` EQUALS `yes: the act could cause or contribute to a covered loss (s 54(2))`
#ASSERT `May the insurer refuse my claim because of what happened after the contract` `leaving the alarm off, part of the loss a storm's` EQUALS `only for the part of the loss the act caused (s 54(4))`
#ASSERT `May the insurer refuse my claim because of what happened after the contract` `driving an injured person to hospital unlicensed` EQUALS `no: the act was needed for safety or to preserve property, or could not reasonably be avoided (s 54(5))`

#ASSERT `How much must the insurer still pay on my claim` 10000 1500 EQUALS 8500

§ `s 40(3), s 56, s 57 -- making the claim, and interest`

#ASSERT `Does my liability insurer still cover the late claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my liability insurer still cover the late claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `What may the insurer do about my claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `refuse it, but not avoid the contract (s 56(1))`

#ASSERT `What is the reg 38 interest rate` 1 4.3 4.1 EQUALS 7.3
#ASSERT `What is the reg 38 interest rate` 2 8.7 4.1 EQUALS 7.25
#ASSERT `What is the reg 38 interest rate` 0 0 4.1 EQUALS 7.1

#ASSERT `How much interest must the insurer pay me` 10000 6 (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `How much interest must the insurer pay me` 10000 7.25 (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 11 9 2026) EQUALS 145

